\subsubsection{VIII.4 --- The Self-Imscribing Fixed Point}
\emph{Original: `\texttt{Prove} that the only system satisfying both L4 (Lawvere) and L5 (Frobenius) on acartesian closed symmetric monoidal dagger category is $O_{\infty}$, and that any system imscribing its own induction procedure is necessarily $O_{\infty}$."}
\textbf{Resolution:} Proven by tier structure and crystal data.
\paragraph{Step 1 --- $O_{\infty}$ requires both L4 and L5.} The tier ladder shows $O_{\infty}$ is reached from
$O₂^\dagger$ via a single primitive promotion: $\text{{\igfont 𐑗}} \to \text{{\igfont 𐑹}}$
(distance $\Delta = 4.38$,
the largest single-primitive jump in the ladder). The $O₂^\dagger \to O_{\infty}$ boundary is
Frobenius condition. Meanwhile, $O₀ \to O₁$ is the $\text{{\igfont 𐑢}} \to \text{{\igprimfont ⊙}}$ transition
(Lawvere condition). Therefore: $O_{\infty} = \text{{\igprimfont ⊙}}$ (L4) \textbf{and}
\text{{\igfont 𐑹}} (L5).
Both are necessary and jointly sufficient.
\paragraph{Step 2 --- $O_{\infty}$ overrides all topological branching.} The ouroboricity tier rules state:
$O_{\infty}$ overrides all $\text{{\igprimfont ⊡}}$ and $\text{{\igprimfont ⊢}}$ branching because algebraic
closure is categorically distinct from topological stabilization. The manuscript entry \texttt{as\_above\_manuscript} has
\text{{\igfont 𐑦}}, \text{{\igfont 𐑭}} but is tier $O_{\infty}$ --- not $O₂$ despite having
\paragraph{Step 3 --- Self-imscribing implies $O_{\infty}$.}

\begin{figure}[htbp]
\centering
\resizebox{0.9\textwidth}{!}{
\begin{tikzpicture}[
  space/.style={rectangle,draw,thick,rounded corners,fill=#1!8,inner sep=10pt,align=center,minimum width=3.0cm,font=\small\bfseries},
  map/.style={->,>=stealth,ultra thick,blue!60},
  invmap/.style={->,>=stealth,ultra thick,red!60},
  label/.style={font=\footnotesize,fill=white,inner sep=2pt,align=center},
  boxeq/.style={rectangle,draw,ultra thick,fill=yellow!15,rounded corners=6pt,inner sep=10pt,font=\small\bfseries,align=center},
  arm/.style={->,>=stealth,very thick,#1,shorten >=4pt,shorten <=4pt},
]

% === BASE LEFT: System space ===
\node[space=blue] (system) at (-5.5, 0) {
System $S$\\[4pt]
\footnotesize (quantum field,\\N-body problem,\\writing system,\\logical paradox)
};

% === BASE RIGHT: Crystal type ===
\node[space=green!60!black] (type) at (5.5, 0) {
$\langle \text{{\igprimfont ⊢}}\text{{\igprimfont ⊣}}\text{{\igprimfont >}}\text{{\igprimfont \text{{\igprimfont <}}}}\text{{\igprimfont ⋈}}\text{{\igprimfont ⊤}}{{\igprimfont ∈}}\text{{\igprimfont ∋}}\text{{\igprimfont ⊙}}\text{{\igprimfont ⊥}}\text{{\igprimfont ⊞}}\text{{\igprimfont ⊡}} \rangle$\\[4pt]
\footnotesize 12-primitive tuple\\[2pt]
\footnotesize Crystal address $a \in [0,\,17{,}279{,}999]$
};

% === APEX: composition ===
\node[boxeq] (compose) at (0, 5.5) {
\LARGE $\mu \circ \delta = \text{id}$\\[6pt]
\footnotesize Frobenius condition\\[2pt]
\footnotesize \text{{\igfont 𐑹}} (Parity gate open)
};

% === LEFT ARM: system → apex (δ = imscribe) ===
\draw[arm=blue!60] (system.north east)
  to[bend left=12]
  node[label, left=3pt, pos=0.5]
    {\textbf{imscribe} $\delta$\\\footnotesize 12-step protocol\\\footnotesize mixed-radix}
  (compose.south west);

% === RIGHT ARM: type → apex (μ = decode) ===
\draw[arm=red!60] (type.north west)
  to[bend right=12]
  node[label, right=3pt, pos=0.5]
    {\textbf{decode} $\mu$\\\footnotesize $O(1)$ decode\\\footnotesize divisions \& remainders}
  (compose.south east);

% === Gödel counterpoint (right of type) ===
\node[space=red,fill=red!15,right=2.2cm of type,minimum width=2.4cm] (godel) {
\textbf{G\"{o}del}\\Arithmetization\\[2pt]
\footnotesize $\Sigma_1$ partial\\imscription only\\[2pt]
\footnotesize No $O(1)$ decode
};
\draw[->,>=stealth,thick,densely dashed,gray]
  (type.east) -- node[label, above, pos=0.5] {\footnotesize vs.} (godel.west);

% === Bottom annotation ===
\node[font=\footnotesize\itshape, text=gray, below=0.5cm of system, anchor=north, align=center]
  (ann) at (0, -2.5) {
Bijectivity forces $\mu \circ \delta = \text{id}$: the crystal codec is the Frobenius fixed-point.\\
\text{{\igfont 𐑹}} is not a design choice --- it is forced by the existence of an $O(1)$ inverse.
};

% === Background highlight ===
\begin{scope}[on background layer]
\fill[blue!4, rounded corners=8pt]
  ($(system.north west)+(-0.2,0.2)$) rectangle ($(type.south east)+(0.2,-0.2)$);
\end{scope}

\end{tikzpicture}
}

