143	
144	The powers of two meet \Cref{thm:main} with equality: $\{1,2,\dots,2^{n-1}\}$
145	has $\Sigma = 2^n - 1$. No set with distinct subset sums can do better against
146	this particular counting argument, because the argument only ever uses that
147	$2^{|A|}$ things are packed injectively into $\Sigma + 1$ slots, and the powers
